# EXWM Setup Guide for Emacs on WSL2

Date: 2026-08-19

## What is EXWM?

EXWM (Emacs X Window Manager) turns Emacs into your entire window manager. Chrome and other applications become Emacs buffers you can switch between with `C-x b`.

---

## Prerequisites

### 1. Check X Server on WSL2

```bash
# Check if DISPLAY is set
echo $DISPLAY

# Test X11 with a simple app
xeyes  # Should open a window with eyes
```

**If DISPLAY is not set:**

```bash
# For WSLg (built-in to WSL2)
export DISPLAY=:0

# Or if using VcXsrv on Windows
export DISPLAY=$(cat /etc/resolv.conf | grep nameserver | awk '{print $2}'):0.0

# Add to ~/.zshrc to make permanent
echo 'export DISPLAY=:0' >> ~/.zshrc
```

### 2. Install Chrome/Chromium

```bash
# Check if installed
which google-chrome || which chromium-browser

# Install if missing
sudo apt update
sudo apt install chromium-browser
```

